Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is a clinical-tool.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline should improve a clinician-patient-communication.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline should support an informed-person-centered-pain-care-decision.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline applies to a primary-care-clinician.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline applies to a pain-care-clinician.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline applies to an adult-outpatient that has a pain that lasts for less than 1 month.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline applies to an adult-outpatient that has a pain that lasts for at least 1 month for at most 3 months.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline applies to an adult-outpatient that has a pain that lasts for more than 3 months.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is a flexible-guideline.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline should support a person-centered-decision.
Every clinician should consider an expected-health-outcome during a person-centered-decision.
Every clinician should consider a well-being during a person-centered-decision.
